    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full test suite passes: **45 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned owner identity so the `customerCode` is now `<REGION>-<HASH8>` with sequence numbers dropped, and cascaded that to every value derived from it.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 replaced `nextCustomerCode(city, lastName)` (which built `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` from a per-city counter) with `customerCode(city, postcode, normalizedTelephone, lastName)`:\n- `REGION` = `Localities.forCityAndPostcode(city, postcode)` \u2014 postcode-first derivation (NSW/VIC/QLD ranges) falling back to the city, matching the region the locality uses.\n- `HASH8` = first 8 upper-case hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalizedTelephone + lastName` (added a `sha256UpperHex` helper). It's called after telephone normalization, so the hash uses the stored E.164 value \u2014 exactly what the tests recompute from the response.\n\nDownstream values needed no formula changes because they already read `customerCode`, so they automatically move to the new identity:\n- **Membership number** (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`) and its **Luhn check digit** in `OwnerMapper`.\n- **Create audit record**, which already logs `owner.getCustomerCode()`.\n\n**`Localities.java` / `OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 moved the **locality derivation** onto the new identity: added `Localities.forOwner(owner)`, which returns the `<REGION>` prefix of the `customerCode`, with a null-safe fallback to `forCityAndPostcode` for owners with no code yet (e.g. seed data). The mapper's `locality` mapping now calls it.\n\nAll 32 checkpoint tests plus the rest of the suite are green.",
